# Where this deployment's names resolve.  hosts(5) format: address, then names.
#
# Four addresses, and they are the whole of what used to be the
# CONTROLLER_LB / GATEWAY_*_LB substitution pass: the manifests now carry names
# and are never edited.  k8s-deploy.sh turns this into `hostAliases` on the
# controller and gateway pods of every cloud — each of them dials the others —
# and `./k8s-deploy.sh -d multi --print-hosts` prints it for the three UPF
# hosts' own /etc/hosts.
#
# Fill these in after the LoadBalancers exist, one cluster at a time:
#
#     kubectl --context <ctx> -n volantis get svc ctrl-svc gateway-svc
#
# All three clusters and all three UPF hosts must agree on these
# values.  That is the point of them being in one file.

# <address>        <name>
# 203.0.113.10     ctrl.volantis.lab
# 203.0.113.11     gw-central.volantis.lab
# 198.51.100.11    gw-edge1.volantis.lab
# 192.0.2.11       gw-edge2.volantis.lab
